# =============================================================================
# i2_mof — default-deny ALLOWLIST .gitignore
#
# This tree is ~623 GB of Quantum ESPRESSO data, almost all of it regenerable
# binaries (wavefunctions .wfc*, charge-density.dat, .save/ restart dirs, .cube
# grids, .mix*, .hdf5, pseudopotentials, ...). Rather than maintain a fragile
# blocklist of every binary type — and re-edit it every time QE emits a new one
# — we invert it:
#
#   1. `*`              ignore everything
#   2. `!*/`            ...but traverse into every directory
#   3. `!<extensions>`  re-allow ONLY known-good text/code/result/figure types
#   4. `/dir/**`        exclude a few scratch/third-party subtrees
#
# Net effect: ONLY the file types in section 3 can ever enter git, no matter
# what new binary extensions appear as the project runs. New calculations get
# their .in/.out/POSCAR/code tracked automatically and their binaries + .save/
# restart dirs ignored automatically — zero manual maintenance.
#
# Gotcha baked into the design: a bare directory pattern like `/tools/` does
# NOT exclude once `!*/` (step 2) is present; the file-level form `/tools/**`
# is required. Verified empirically against `git add`.
# =============================================================================

# --- 1. Ignore everything by default ---
*

# --- 2. Traverse into every directory so the allowlist below can match ---
!*/

# --- 3. ALLOWLIST (the only file types that can be tracked) ---
# repo meta
!/.gitignore
# code
!*.py
!*.sh
!*.pl
# docs / text / structured data
!*.md
!*.rst
!*.txt
!*.json
!*.yaml
!*.yml
!*.csv
!*.tsv
!*.tex
# QE / VASP inputs and text outputs
!*.in
!*.out
!*.pwi
!*.pwo
# structures
!*.cif
!*.xyz
!*.vasp
!*POSCAR*
!KPOINTS*
!INCAR*
# figures / tables
!*.pdf
!*.png
!*.jpg
!*.jpeg
!*.svg
!*.eps
!*.docx
!*.xlsx

# --- 4. EXCLUDE subtrees (file-level /** ; MUST follow the allowlist).
#        NOTE: gitignore has NO inline comments — a '#' mid-line is taken
#        literally and silently breaks the pattern. Keep comments on their
#        own '#' lines, patterns alone on theirs.
# third-party binaries/source: critic2, multiwfn, tarballs
/tools/**
# scratch
/tmp/**
# redundant copy of final_activated_results/
/final_activated_results_archive/**
# QE .save/ restart dirs (any depth; covers future runs automatically)
*.save/
# QE PAW numeric dump inside .save/ (the only allowlisted type that lives there)
paw.txt
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo

# --- Tunables: uncomment a line to START tracking that type ---
# !*.upf     # pseudopotentials (treated as external: PSLibrary / SSSP)
# !*.xml     # QE data-file-schema dumps (regenerable)
# !*.log     # run / campaign logs
